loglan-tools: who owns what
===========================

This repository holds two kinds of file, under different terms.


1. LOGLAN MATERIAL -- OWNED BY THE LOGLAN CENTER, INC.
   NOT covered by the GPL.  All rights reserved by The Loglan Center.

    sources/Dictionary/L-to-E-TDR.html
                    Lavinia Randall Holmes's Loglan-to-English dictionary
    sources/Loglan1/*
                    Loglan 1, by James Cooke Brown, HTML edition
    sources/Sources/omnibus.py
                    Randall Holmes's PEG parser for Loglan
    lists/utts      the sentences of the Institute's LoglanTeach and MacTeach
                    programs, corrected to current Loglan grammar
    lists/aux/ethnic
    lists/aux/animals
                    the ethnic and animal declension sets, drawn from the
                    dictionary
    loglan-teach/new-words-html.py -- the page template only
                    the HEAD and FOOT strings, between the lines marked
                    "The Loglan Center's material", taken from the
                    Loglan-to-English dictionary's own pages

   Also Loglan material: everything the programs build from it in your data
   directory (~/.loglan) -- the word lists, the cheat sheet, the dictionary
   pages -- except your own words.

   All rights to this material are reserved by The Loglan Center, Inc. (the
   Idaho corporation which has superseded the Florida corporation).  It is
   included with The Loglan Center's permission, given by Lavinia Randall
   Holmes in October 2026:

       "I have no problem with your using current Loglan materials.  Just
       include the statement that all rights are reserved by The Loglan
       Center, Inc (the Idaho corporation which has superseded the Florida
       corporation).  Our general view is that a language should be used,
       not hoarded."

   The originals are published at
   <https://randall-holmes.github.io/Loglan/cefli.html>; sources/MANIFEST
   gives the address, checksum and date of each copy here.  Each of these
   files, or its directory, says the same in a notice of its own
   (sources/NOTICE; the header of each list; the marked lines in
   new-words-html.py).


